extends layout

block content
  section.projects
    .container
      h1.section-title Projects

      .projects-grid
        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Personal Website
          p.project-description
            | You're looking at it! This is my digital home—a place to share my work, write about what I'm learning,
            | and make it easy for people to get in touch. It's fast, clean, and feels smooth to navigate.
          p.project-description.tech-details
            | Built with a NestJS backend serving server-rendered Pug templates for SEO benefits. The blog system
            | parses Markdown files with syntax highlighting via highlight.js. Page transitions use the View Transitions API
            | with GSAP animations, while the contact form integrates Zoho Mail OAuth2 with hCaptcha spam protection
            | and XSS sanitisation.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/jordancolehunt.com`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Pug
            span.tag Vanilla JS
            span.tag Markdown
            span.tag Zoho Mail
            span.tag GSAP
            span.tag highlight.js

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Vertical Lane Racer
          p.project-description
            | A retro-style racing game that runs right in your terminal. Four AI drivers compete to dodge obstacles
            | and cross the finish line first. It's built twice—once in JavaScript, once in Python—as a way to explore
            | how modern features in each language compare when solving the same problem.
            strong  (Work in Progress)
          p.project-description.tech-details
            | Demonstrates feature parity between ES2020+ JavaScript (private fields, generators, Set.difference)
            | and Python 3.10+ (type hints, pattern matching, dataclasses, protocols). Uses the strategy pattern
            | for AI decision-making with full state serialisation, making it ready for LLM or vision model integration.
            | Async/await handles concurrent updates with ANSI terminal rendering at 10 FPS.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/race-sim`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag JavaScript
            span.tag Python
            span.tag Node.js
            span.tag Async/Await
            span.tag Strategy Pattern
            span.tag Terminal UI
            span.tag Generators
            span.tag Type Safety

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Dino Park
          p.project-description
            | Ever wanted to run a dinosaur park without the risk of being eaten? This simulation lets you manage
            | a grid of enclosures, keeping track of feeding schedules, dinosaur movements, and maintenance alerts.
            | Real-time events keep things unpredictable—just like the real thing, minus the velociraptors.
          p.project-description.tech-details
            | Built with pure functional programming principles in React. Processes real-time events from an external API
            | to manage a 26×16 park grid using immutable data structures throughout. Features a three-panel UI
            | with safety indicators and comprehensive Vitest coverage demonstrating clean functional architecture.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/dino-park`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag React
            span.tag Vite
            span.tag Vitest
            span.tag JavaScript
            span.tag Functional Programming
            span.tag Immutable Data
